Models
------
Accio does not include any model weights. They are downloaded from Hugging Face
at first use and are governed by their own licenses:

- mlx-community/embeddinggemma-300m-bf16, an MLX conversion of Google's
  EmbeddingGemma. Used for all retrieval. Subject to the Gemma Terms of Use:
  https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms

- gaudi/opus-mt-en-de-ctranslate2 and gaudi/opus-mt-de-en-ctranslate2,
  CTranslate2 conversions of Helsinki-NLP's opus-mt-en-de and opus-mt-de-en.
  Used to search each question in both German and English (ACCIO_TRANSLATE=0
  turns this off). Licensed CC-BY-4.0 by the Language Technology Research
  Group at the University of Helsinki: https://huggingface.co/Helsinki-NLP

- mlx-community/Qwen2.5-VL-3B-Instruct-4bit, an MLX conversion of
  Qwen/Qwen2.5-VL-3B-Instruct. Used only when image captions are switched on
  (ACCIO_CAPTION=1, off by default). The upstream model card lists the
  Qwen Research License (research and non-commercial use):
  https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2.5-VL-3B-Instruct/blob/main/LICENSE

Name
----
"Accio" is the summoning charm from J.K. Rowling's Harry Potter books, used here
as an affectionate reference. This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
or connected to J.K. Rowling, Warner Bros., or any Harry Potter rights holder.
The icon is original artwork.

